WEBVTT

00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:08.357
Instead of staying in St. Paul academy
and becoming a lady on the surface,

00:00:08.529 --> 00:00:12.251
Candy decided that she would rather leave
in order to find her own path in life.

00:00:13.528 --> 00:00:14.726
And,

00:00:14.823 --> 00:00:19.584
After asking director Gray to amend Eliza's
week-long room confinement,

00:00:19.797 --> 00:00:25.604
...on the following morning, Candy quickly left,
leaving the school's premises after herself.

00:00:30.324 --> 00:00:36.418
Long way to the port.

00:01:00.382 --> 00:01:02.022
Grandfather William.

00:01:02.407 --> 00:01:06.968
Thank you for adopting someone of my kind.

00:01:07.814 --> 00:01:11.130
Today, I am renouncing the adoption
by the Adley family.

00:01:11.683 --> 00:01:17.191
I realized that up until now, I've been
relying too much on the Adley family.

00:01:17.793 --> 00:01:22.149
From now on, I want to find my own path
with my own strength.

00:01:22.563 --> 00:01:26.215
Please, forgive me for failing to become a lady.

00:01:26.916 --> 00:01:30.841
I will never, ever forget Grandfather's kindness.

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:43.563
Let's go, Kurin!

00:01:52.606 --> 00:01:57.965
Eliza Leagan. I am amending your punishment.
You will participate in classes again.

00:01:59.121 --> 00:02:03.539
Duke Grandchester must have received the
letter I secretly sent him.

00:02:04.151 --> 00:02:05.353
Eliza Leagan.

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:08.607
You might be fond of sending letters that
are meant to trouble other people,

00:02:09.104 --> 00:02:10.841
...but doing so isn't a good thing.

00:02:11.148 --> 00:02:12.696
Be careful from now on.

00:02:15.688 --> 00:02:16.487
This is...

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:18.975
The letter I sent to Duke Grandchester!

00:02:21.771 --> 00:02:23.492
Sister... sister Gray!

00:02:23.633 --> 00:02:26.787
Sister Margaret, what happened?
Barging in like that, without knocking...!

00:02:26.799 --> 00:02:30.786
Excuse my rudeness, sister Gray,
but Candice White Adley has...

00:02:31.492 --> 00:02:33.212
Something happened to Candice?

00:02:33.492 --> 00:02:35.207
She left school!

00:02:35.494 --> 00:02:36.776
Candy has...?

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:39.322
Sister! We received her letters, too!

00:02:39.532 --> 00:02:41.810
Calm down!
Don't make this much noise.

00:02:42.345 --> 00:02:43.869
-Sister Gray!
-Annie?

00:02:44.029 --> 00:02:46.086
-You are here about Candy, too?
-Yes!

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:49.592
Sister Gray, we'd like to offer our help!

00:02:49.834 --> 00:02:50.837
What would you do?

00:02:51.235 --> 00:02:54.036
What do you mean? Of course,
we'd bring Candy back!

00:02:54.309 --> 00:02:56.103
Why would you do such a thing?

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:59.820
She left on her own will, so she
doesn't want to be brought back!

00:03:00.193 --> 00:03:02.203
Eliza! You...

00:03:02.859 --> 00:03:08.918
Sister Gray, anyway, we'll take a look
around the school premises. Now, let's go!

00:03:09.125 --> 00:03:10.082
We'll go as well!

00:03:10.425 --> 00:03:11.545
Wait!

00:03:16.427 --> 00:03:19.995
Sister Gray, Candy needs to be expelled.

00:03:21.004 --> 00:03:24.947
Sister Gray, I'm sure that Candy went after Terry.

00:03:24.982 --> 00:03:26.237
You are wrong.

00:03:27.664 --> 00:03:30.688
Candice left me a letter, as well.

00:03:42.678 --> 00:03:46.050
Good thing I secretly made these sandwiches
during the night, Kurin!

00:04:44.588 --> 00:04:45.282
What's the matter?!

00:04:45.446 --> 00:04:47.394
Stop!

00:04:50.295 --> 00:04:51.867
Hey! Calm down!

00:05:11.546 --> 00:05:13.226
What's the matter? Are you hurt?

00:05:13.603 --> 00:05:15.767
No, I'm fine.
Sorry.

00:05:17.882 --> 00:05:20.651
You'll catch a cold like that.
You'd better change quickly.

00:05:20.890 --> 00:05:23.424
I'm sorry for boarding your carriage
without asking...

00:05:23.777 --> 00:05:27.325
-It's okay! Now, hurry!
-Thank you.

00:05:27.533 --> 00:05:29.370
I'm Candy!

00:05:29.491 --> 00:05:32.058
I'm Arnold.
Nice to meet you.

00:05:54.193 --> 00:05:55.759
-Hurry up, brother!
-Okay!

00:06:03.203 --> 00:06:06.214
-They're cute!
-C'mon, hurry up...

00:06:06.723 --> 00:06:08.512
Alright! Go!

00:06:16.294 --> 00:06:21.276
By the way, Candy, you still haven't
told me where you're heading to.

00:06:21.467 --> 00:06:25.995
Oh, I still haven't mentioned that?
I'd like to go to the port and board a ship!

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:30.132
To the port? I can take you halfway,
are you okay with that?

00:06:30.302 --> 00:06:33.312
Yes please, mr. Arnold!
I would appreciate that!

00:07:19.775 --> 00:07:20.920
We made it in time!

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:25.341
Candy!

00:07:25.403 --> 00:07:26.656
Candy!

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:27.774
Candy!

00:07:28.137 --> 00:07:28.997
Candy!

00:07:33.005 --> 00:07:33.968
What's going on?

00:07:34.283 --> 00:07:35.504
I'm sorry, mister!

00:07:41.287 --> 00:07:45.970
Candice White Adley?
I don't remember seeing that name in the register.

00:08:01.628 --> 00:08:03.763
Candy is nowhere to be found.

00:08:04.055 --> 00:08:05.947
Maybe she is hiding somewhere.

00:08:06.510 --> 00:08:11.465
Sister Margaret, I owe you so much.
Please, forgive me for leaving without seeing you.

00:08:11.838 --> 00:08:14.970
Stear, Archie; I'm sorry for leaving
out of my own accord.

00:08:15.539 --> 00:08:20.109
Annie, Patty; I quietly left because I didn't
want to cry while bidding you farewell.

00:08:23.610 --> 00:08:26.668
Candy... I'm sure we'll see each other again!

00:08:26.748 --> 00:08:29.624
That's why... I'm not going to bid you farewell!

00:08:53.477 --> 00:08:55.087
Huh? Where are we?

00:08:56.428 --> 00:08:57.746
You woke up?

00:08:57.953 --> 00:09:00.908
How far is it till Southampton port?

00:09:00.946 --> 00:09:04.324
Huh? You meant the port in Southampton?

00:09:04.406 --> 00:09:05.178
Yes...

00:09:06.261 --> 00:09:08.468
We are going in the opposite direction.

00:09:10.124 --> 00:09:13.786
I thought you wanted to go to the port in Dover.

00:09:14.061 --> 00:09:16.496
Can I travel to America from Dover?

00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:20.007
No, you can only go to America from Southampton.

00:09:20.187 --> 00:09:21.866
Then, if I hurry now...

00:09:21.902 --> 00:09:23.346
You're in such a hurry?

00:09:23.941 --> 00:09:26.114
Uh, it's not that I'm in a hurry...

00:09:26.364 --> 00:09:32.382
It's almost night. If you aren't in such a hurry,
you can stay overnight at my place. We're almost there.

00:09:43.983 --> 00:09:45.929
Pinky! Attaboy!

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:49.683
This time I'll stay at home tonight!

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:52.748
Mr. Arnold, you're a shepherd?

00:09:53.364 --> 00:09:56.464
That's right.
Pinky, look what a cute guest we have.

00:09:56.663 --> 00:09:59.418
Nice to meet you, Pinky!
This is Kurin.

00:10:00.967 --> 00:10:02.213
Kurin, what's the matter?

00:10:04.203 --> 00:10:05.450
This Pinky...

00:10:10.308 --> 00:10:12.658
-Well, Candy, why don't you come in?
-Yes!

00:10:15.183 --> 00:10:16.900
Come, Pinky, Kurin!

00:10:23.902 --> 00:10:26.744
*Denjin Anime Fansub*
Hey, audio is good again.

00:10:38.286 --> 00:10:39.850
All the leaves are falling...

00:10:40.083 --> 00:10:40.715
Yeah.

00:10:41.014 --> 00:10:42.955
I wonder what's Candy doing now.

00:10:43.195 --> 00:10:43.999
Yeah.

00:10:56.768 --> 00:10:57.712
Ow!

00:10:57.747 --> 00:10:59.842
-Annie, are you okay?
-Yeah...

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:05.429
-You haven't knitted anything for a while...
-Patty, and you keep staring at the same page...

00:11:06.937 --> 00:11:10.506
Candy... you parted from us with such a short letter...

00:11:10.919 --> 00:11:17.439
Annie, we should become stronger from now on.
We shouldn't give Candy a reason to worry about us.

00:11:17.981 --> 00:11:21.002
Yes... Candy hates crybabies.

00:11:21.564 --> 00:11:22.739
That's right.

00:11:35.085 --> 00:11:37.962
Kurin! You still have a lot to learn!

00:11:38.065 --> 00:11:41.494
-Oh? A sheep went astray again.
-Leave it to me!

00:11:54.468 --> 00:11:56.271
Thank you!

00:11:57.443 --> 00:12:00.506
It looks though I'm better at these things
than at being a lady!

00:12:06.325 --> 00:12:08.534
I haven't felt alive in such a long time!

00:12:09.268 --> 00:12:11.822
You make it sound
like you were asleep for a long time.

00:12:11.972 --> 00:12:15.845
Yeah. I feel as if I were asleep
ever since I arrived to England.

00:12:16.240 --> 00:12:18.262
And today, I finally woke up!

00:12:18.780 --> 00:12:21.044
I'm going to begin anew!

00:12:22.142 --> 00:12:26.296
Really, Candy, you look like you
escaped from a long torment.

00:12:26.666 --> 00:12:28.803
Your eyes are all glittery!

00:12:29.385 --> 00:12:32.591
I'm so glad I escaped!

00:12:34.386 --> 00:12:37.629
Miss Candice left this letter for mr. William?

00:12:38.079 --> 00:12:41.117
Yes. I am very sorry that
such a thing happened.

00:12:41.152 --> 00:12:42.915
No, it's not your fault.

00:12:43.145 --> 00:12:45.489
Miss Candice wrote that in her letter.

00:12:46.748 --> 00:12:48.356
I am worried about one thing, however.

00:12:48.505 --> 00:12:51.569
Miss Candice took off with almost no money.

00:12:51.954 --> 00:12:52.616
Money?

00:12:52.653 --> 00:12:57.197
It's too late now, but I was afraid that such a thing
might happen so I personally brought this...

00:12:59.147 --> 00:13:02.094
So Candice went on a journey completely penniless.

00:13:05.024 --> 00:13:08.369
Farewell, mr. Arnold, Pinky!

00:13:08.521 --> 00:13:11.846
Stay well, Candy!

00:13:18.518 --> 00:13:22.632
Kurin, it's just you and me from now on.
Our new beginning.

00:13:23.554 --> 00:13:24.609
Let's go, Kurin!

00:13:39.366 --> 00:13:41.335
It's raining. Kurin, let's hurry!

00:13:58.957 --> 00:14:02.418
Kurin, I'm hungry.
I'll buy us some food.

00:14:03.407 --> 00:14:06.324
Welcome!
How can I help you, miss?

00:14:07.589 --> 00:14:10.210
Can I get something to eat
for ten shillings?

00:14:10.546 --> 00:14:11.860
Ten shillings?

00:14:11.936 --> 00:14:14.742
You can't buy much for ten shillings.

00:14:15.913 --> 00:14:19.365
I know. Give me your cheapest bread then!

00:14:22.275 --> 00:14:23.323
Alright.

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:25.884
Here! You can take this.

00:14:26.099 --> 00:14:27.848
Really? It's pretty big...

00:14:28.554 --> 00:14:31.348
-It's okay. Take it.
-Thank you!

00:14:41.807 --> 00:14:47.295
Kurin, I'm sorry. I'll find a proper job
tomorrow, so please bear it for tonight.

00:14:51.159 --> 00:14:53.457
I won't give up, Terry!

00:15:06.103 --> 00:15:09.302
I'll look for a job in that town!
Let's go, Kurin!

00:15:12.787 --> 00:15:20.128
Nah, I don't need any help.
As you can see, I can manage everything on my own.

00:15:20.320 --> 00:15:23.241
That's right, you need a job...

00:15:23.956 --> 00:15:26.433
We don't hire women.

00:15:33.474 --> 00:15:40.063
This isn't good. I'm broke, couldn't find a job,
and I'm hungry. Are we going to sleep out again?

00:15:43.355 --> 00:15:45.050
Kurin, you're hungry too?

00:15:45.405 --> 00:15:47.967
Alright! I'll keep looking for a job!

00:15:53.048 --> 00:15:56.909
Bed and breakfast.
Maybe I could work at this inn.

00:16:00.005 --> 00:16:01.303
Welcome!

00:16:03.330 --> 00:16:04.450
Uh...

00:16:04.657 --> 00:16:05.580
What is it?

00:16:06.342 --> 00:16:09.149
Uh... would you let me work here
just for one night?

00:16:09.760 --> 00:16:11.110
Let me work...

00:16:17.024 --> 00:16:20.212
Looks like you have a reason.
Your working experience?

00:16:20.796 --> 00:16:23.597
Yes... I used to work in kitchen.

00:16:24.557 --> 00:16:27.874
-Just for this night...
-Please!

00:16:28.724 --> 00:16:30.459
You won't earn a lot.

00:16:30.873 --> 00:16:32.951
I'm willing to work for a meal alone.

00:16:34.513 --> 00:16:37.319
Well, let's see what you can do.
Come.

00:16:37.791 --> 00:16:39.268
Thank goodness...

00:16:39.643 --> 00:16:41.062
Are you okay?

00:16:42.057 --> 00:16:43.467
I'm fine!

00:16:46.768 --> 00:16:51.276
I didn't know I would make use of experience
I got while working in Eliza's kitchen.

00:16:52.351 --> 00:16:54.140
-Are you done?
-Yes.

00:16:54.279 --> 00:16:57.814
-Well, I prepared a meal for you.
-Thank you!

00:17:05.489 --> 00:17:07.134
Kurin, you!

00:17:09.923 --> 00:17:11.243
Please...

00:17:11.543 --> 00:17:12.681
Please...

00:17:13.604 --> 00:17:15.110
Have mercy...

00:17:15.158 --> 00:17:17.776
We don't have anything!
Get out!

00:17:18.215 --> 00:17:19.906
Something to eat...

00:17:19.941 --> 00:17:22.247
I told you, we don't have anything!

00:17:24.252 --> 00:17:25.818
Have mercy...

00:17:28.028 --> 00:17:31.144
See, this girl worked hard for it.

00:17:31.445 --> 00:17:35.362
You just want people to give you things
instead of having to work for them!

00:17:36.330 --> 00:17:38.020
Have mercy...

00:17:47.014 --> 00:17:49.208
Thank you, kind lady!

00:18:00.569 --> 00:18:02.293
Thank you, miss!

00:18:03.935 --> 00:18:07.262
Aren't you a dumb one!
I thought you were hungry!

00:18:07.297 --> 00:18:08.171
Yeah...

00:18:08.345 --> 00:18:11.375
Why'd you do that?

00:18:11.417 --> 00:18:12.859
I felt sorry for him...

00:18:13.300 --> 00:18:15.131
What will you do now?

00:18:15.525 --> 00:18:17.362
Please let me work more!

00:18:18.057 --> 00:18:22.967
You're quite something...
Okay, okay, eat all you want.

00:18:23.622 --> 00:18:29.583
Listen to me. I don't know your circumstances,
but I want you to know that living alone is hard!

00:18:29.676 --> 00:18:31.619
-Don't take it too lightly!
-Yes!

00:18:32.004 --> 00:18:35.273
If you understood me, eat up.
I'll let you stay here for tonight.

00:18:35.274 --> 00:18:39.194
-But I don't have money...
-It's okay. You don't plan on staying, anyway.

00:18:40.347 --> 00:18:41.575
I...

00:18:42.273 --> 00:18:48.086
Now, now, if you cried over such a little thing,
what will happen from now on? There, there!

00:18:58.119 --> 00:19:03.376
Terry, mr. Albert! I finally
started treading my own path.

00:19:03.829 --> 00:19:07.852
I feel so much more human
since I left St. Paul academy.

00:19:08.333 --> 00:19:12.446
The landlady has quite a big mouth,
but she is actually a very good person!

00:19:14.562 --> 00:19:16.444
Good night, everyone!

00:19:23.106 --> 00:19:24.431
Good morning!

00:19:24.875 --> 00:19:26.700
Oh? You're up already?

00:19:26.877 --> 00:19:28.509
I wanted to bake some bread.

00:19:29.350 --> 00:19:30.618
You can bake bread?

00:19:31.159 --> 00:19:34.123
Yes. A cook taught me how to.

00:19:36.488 --> 00:19:38.451
You're quite something.

00:19:47.821 --> 00:19:50.561
It's good! You're quite something, Candy!

00:19:50.957 --> 00:19:53.158
I'm glad you like it!

00:19:56.192 --> 00:19:57.748
Thank you for waiting!

00:19:58.420 --> 00:20:01.912
-Hey, Candy, the stew is done!
-Yes!

00:20:05.105 --> 00:20:08.652
Really, she is such a good girl...
Cheerful, hard-working...

00:20:09.851 --> 00:20:11.217
Thank you for waiting!

00:20:22.164 --> 00:20:23.532
Thank you.

00:20:23.931 --> 00:20:25.468
You helped me so much.

00:20:25.863 --> 00:20:27.481
Must you really go?

00:20:28.420 --> 00:20:33.150
Yes. I plan on working and saving some money
while going to Southampton.

00:20:33.740 --> 00:20:36.425
Uh, here, don't mind it,
it's just to cover some of your expenses.

00:20:36.816 --> 00:20:38.676
But... you don't have to.

00:20:38.888 --> 00:20:42.641
It's your salary for baking that bread.
Take it!

00:20:42.742 --> 00:20:43.982
Thank you!

00:20:45.675 --> 00:20:46.986
Take care!

00:20:47.961 --> 00:20:48.676
I will!

00:20:52.202 --> 00:20:54.810
Farewell! Stay well!

00:20:55.375 --> 00:20:56.537
Farewell!

00:21:02.513 --> 00:21:07.935
Candy wasn't sure whether she would
really make it back to her homeland, Pony's home.

00:21:08.708 --> 00:21:11.459
However, she couldn't turn back anymore.

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:15.261
She pressed forward, never looking back.

00:21:17.260 --> 00:21:20.324
To be continued.
